\subsection{\code{BaseRContourLayerProcessor$generate_selectors()}}{
  Address each curve by the element that drew it

gridGraphics writes one \code{lines} grob per curve, named
\verb{graphics-plot-<group>-contour-<i>-<i>}, in the order
\code{contourLines()} returns them -- checked vertex count by vertex
count, not assumed. A \code{lines} grob renders as a \verb{<polyline>}.

Withheld entirely when the count does not match what was announced.
The frontend drops a layer whose selector list disagrees with its
series count, and a partial list would hand a curve its neighbour's
element -- the defect #145 and #204 are both about.
